 "note": "Pen order of every glyph stroke (PEN_SPEC 12.3). Each stroke is a list of waypoints in source px, in the order the pen passes them, read off 12x crops of the photo (a few px accurate). glyphs.py follows the letter's skeleton between consecutive waypoints, so the waypoints fix the route and the direction, never the geometry. 'line': a short bar whose skeleton is lost in thinning, drawn straight between its two waypoints and checked against the medial axis like the rest. 'dot': an i-dot, a 1.4 src px tap at the brightest point within 2 px of the waypoint. Words are written left to right, letters in writing order, each i dotted after its word. 'free' (2026-11-07, revision 1): the stroke ends that are not junctions ('s' start, 'e' end); glyphs.py moves each free end to the ink end minus half the stroke width, and the build gates |gap| <= 1 src px. Revision 2 (2026-11-07): the nose-top 219 is drawn again at D and T (without it the plate outline read as a blank band). Its numerals lie on the plate in steep perspective (their 'up' points to the upper right), so each is one stroke of 'parts' joined by corners (a pen stop, no lift): the 2 from its top-left hook over the bowl and down the diagonal, a corner at the bottom-left, then the base (straight); the 1 from its flag's free end to the apex, a corner, then down the stem (both straight); the 9 from the stem junction counter-clockwise round the bowl back to the junction, a corner, then the tail. A 'line' part runs straight from the previous part's end, so no part retraces a thinning spur. Revision 3 (2026-11-07): the side-plate 9 is built the same way as the nose-top 9: from the stem junction up the bowl's right side, over the top, down the left side, round the bottom back to the junction, a corner, then the tail (the revision 2 stroke started on the bowl's right side at y 709 and left 11.6 src px of the bowl, y 709-721, undrawn). The side-plate 1 starts with a short straight lead-in on its flag's tip, which hooks down past where the thinned skeleton stops; 'smooth' joins that part to the next without a corner (no pen stop). 'dot_centre': 'ink' puts an i-dot at the ink centre of the dot instead of its brightest pixel (the 'i' of Olin). Revision 5 (2026-11-09, the main loop's decision): the nose-top 219 is drawn at class D only (PEN_SPEC 3, P3 nose row); at 768 its digits were 7.4-9.0 CSS px tall and read as curls.",
